codex
The manual confirms the `rldimi` wrap case is defined. It also overturns a key premise at Site 2: when `MB > ME`, the 64-bit mask wraps through the high half of RA. A source cast alone therefore leaves `rlwimi` incorrect; the repair must also insert the duplicated rotated word into those high bits.

